 \]
 and $q$ is defined as follows: if $p=0$, then $q=e$; if $0<p<e$ and $p\neq1$, then $q$ is the unique positive number different from $p$ that satisfies $q(\log q-1)=p(\log p-1)$; and if $p\ge e$, then $q=0$.
