\end{equation}
Then using the fiber bundle structure of $f$ and the $C^0_{\loc}$ convergence of $\omega(t)$, arguing as in \cite[Proof of Lemma 9.1]{TWY2}, we can construct a curve $\tilde \gamma$ contained in $X^\circ$, connecting $p$ and $q$, such that
\begin{equation}\label{eq--length upper bound}
