Let $F$ be a strictly 1-balanced graph with $s > 0$ edges on $r \geq 2$ vertices. Then there exist constants $\delta, \varepsilon > 0$ such that the following holds. For any sequences satisfying $p \leq n^{-1/\rd_1(F) + \varepsilon}$ and $q \leq (1 - n^{-\delta})p^{s}$, and for the graphs $G = G(n, p)$ and $R = R_F(n, q)$, there exists a coupling of $G$ and $R$ such that, \whp, there exists a permutation $\tau = \tau(G, R) : [n] \to [n]$ for which every $F(v_1, \ldots, v_r) \in E(R)$ satisfies $F(\tau(v_1), \ldots, \tau(v_r)) \subseteq G$.

