We prove that the consistently oriented double ray is ubiquitous if and only if it is ubiquitous restricted to the class of one-ended digraphs.
Additionally, we prove the same equivalence for the disjoint union of a consistently forward and a consistently backward oriented ray. 
Furthermore, we discuss the connection between these two ubiquity problems.
\end{abstract}

