Suppose $L$ is the closure of a non-split positive braid in $S^3$ with components $L_1,\ldots,L_n$, and assume that at least one component is not the unknot. Then the Dehn surgery along a multislope $(s_1,\ldots,s_n)\in\mathbb{Q}^n$ satisfying $s_i<2g(L_i)-1$ for all $i=1,\ldots,n$ yields a $3$-manifold admitting a co-oriented taut foliation.
