Let $\cM$ be any nondegenerate submanifold of $\R^n$ and $\psi_1,\dots,\psi_n:\Rp\to(0,1)$ be non-increasing. Then almost all points on $\cM$ are $(\psi_1,\dots,\psi_n)$-approximable if the series
\begin{equation}\label{mainsum}
\sum_{q=1}^\infty\psi_1(q)\cdots \psi_n(q)
\end{equation}
diverges, and are not $(\psi_1,\dots,\psi_n)$-approximable if \eqref{mainsum} converges.
\end{theorem}

