\begin{proof}
 The proof of (c) appears in Proposition \ref{prop:ukqdefinesukd}, which also proves (d) and (e). The proofs of $(a)$ and $(b)$ each follow
 by straightforward calculation:
 \begin{multline*}
 (A\ominus B)^T = ((A-I_m\otimes B)\oslash I_n)^T = (A-I_m\otimes B)^T\oslash I_n \\
 = (A^T-I_m\otimes B^T)\oslash I_n = A^T\ominus B^T,
 \end{multline*}
 \begin{multline*}
 \tr(A\ominus B) = \tr((A-I_m\otimes B)\oslash I_n) \\
 = \dfrac{\tr(A-I_m\otimes B)}n
 = \dfrac1n(\tr(A)-m\tr(B)).
 \qedhere
 \end{multline*}
\end{proof}

