Zakharov--Craig--Sulem framework, which we briefly recall below. A more detailed derivation can be seen in, for example, \cite{Wahlen2007HamiltonianConstantVorticity}.  We assume that our free boundary is a graph $\partial\mathcal D(t)=\{(x,y): y=\eta(t,x)\}$. Since the vorticity $\mathrm{curl}\,\mathbf u = \omega$ is a constant, the velocity can be written as a shear flow plus an irrotational perturbation as
\begin{equation}\label{velocity}
