\label{thm}
Let $0\leq f\in C^1([0,1))$ satisfying $F(1)=+\infty$.
Assume that $0\le u\le 1$ is a  stable radial solution to
\begin{align}\label{d-p}
\left\{
\begin{aligned}
-\bdz u & = f(u)&\quad{\rm in}&\quad B_1 \setminus\{ 0\}  \\
u& =0 \quad&{\rm on}&\quad \partial B_1,\\
\end{aligned}
\right.
\end{align}
If $2\le n\le 6$, then $u$ is regular and satisfies
$$\frac 12 u_r(1)^2\le F(\|u\|_{L^\infty(B_1)})\le  Cu_r(1)^2.$$
Additionally, if $f$ is nondecreasing, then
 $$F(\|u\|_{L^\infty(B_1)})\le C,$$
where  $C>0$ is a universal constant.,

