\label{mainth1}
Let $c,d,s\in\mathbb Z^+$ with $d\geq 2$, $1\leq c,s\leq d$ and $\gcd(cs,d)=1$, and let $p\geq5$ be a prime with $p\equiv s\pmod d$. Then, for any $r\in\mathbb Z^+$ with $(\f12+\alpha)^{\ast_r}(\f12+\alpha^{\ast_r})\not\eq0\pmod{p}$,  we have
