[\textsc{Weighted Khintchine for manifolds}]\label{thm: dream0}
Let $\mathcal{M}$ be any nondegenerate submanifold of $\mathbb{R}^n$ and $\psi_1,\dots,\psi_n:\mathbb{R}_+\to(0,1)$ be non-increasing. Then almost all points on $\mathcal{M}$ are $(\psi_1,\dots,\psi_n)$-approximable if the series
\begin{equation}\label{mainsum}
\sum_{q=1}^\infty\psi_1(q)\cdots \psi_n(q)
\end{equation}
diverges, and are not $(\psi_1,\dots,\psi_n)$-approximable if the equation above converges.

