ref_dict.thm-main2:
\begin{thm}\label{thm-main2}
 Let \(M^{4}\) be a K\"ahler-Einstein surface with Einstein constant \(\mathfrak{c}>0\), and let \(x\colon\Sigma \rightarrow M^{4}\) be a complex curve. Then 
 \begin{itemize}
    \item[{\rm(1)}] the first eigenvalue $\Lambda_1$ of its area Jacobi operator is at least $2\mathfrak{c}$,
    \item[{\rm(2)}] if $\Sigma$ has genus $g\leq 1$, then $\Lambda_1=2\mathfrak{c}$ and the corresponding eigenspace has dimension
    \[
    \mathfrak{c}\frac{\operatorname{Area}}{2\pi}+1-g+\dim H^{\,0}(N^*_\Sigma\otimes K_\Sigma^2),
    \]
    where $N^*_\Sigma$ is the dual of the normal bundle, $K_\Sigma$ is the canonical line bundle of $\Sigma$, and $H^{\,0}(N^*_\Sigma\otimes K_\Sigma^2)$ denotes  the space of holomorphic sections of $N^*_\Sigma\otimes K_\Sigma^2$. 
\end{itemize}
\end{thm}

