\begin{equation}\label{eq:pres}\pi_1(M)=\langle h,c_1,c_2,c_3 \ | \  [c_i,h]=1, c_i^{p_i}h^{q_i}=1,  c_1c_2c_3=1\rangle.\end{equation}
together with a theorem of Heusener and Porti (HP23) that, for a finitely generated group $\Gamma,$ gives a presentation of $\C[\X(\Gamma)]$ in terms of a presentation of the group $\Gamma.$ Differentiating the presentation of $\C[\X(M)]$ at an exceptional abelian character $[\rho]$ will give a presentation of the tangent space $T_{[\rho]}\X(M),$ which will be of dimension $1.$ A further differentiation will show that there is no order $2$ deformation of $[\rho].$,

