\end{theorem}

\item "Relying on the fact that all these properties pass to inductive limits," remove the finite-dimensionality hypothesis on $X$.

\item Conclude that proving the main theorem reduces to proving the Global Glimm Property for $C(X,A)$: under condition (1) this follows from \cite[Theorem~4.3]{BlaKir04GlimmHalving}, while under condition (2) it is new and is proved in the following proposition.

