\label{thm_main}
There are the following bijections between sets of respective equivalence classes:
\begin{enumerate}
\item $\{$monoidal bicategories$\}\cong\{\mathsf{E}_1$-algebras in $\mathrm{BiCat}^{\times}\}$;
\item $\{$braided monoidal bicategories$\}\cong\{\mathsf{E}_2$-algebras in $\mathrm{BiCat}^{\times}\}$;
\item $\{$sylleptic monoidal bicategories$\}\cong\{\mathsf{E}_3$-algebras in $\mathrm{BiCat}^{\times}\}$;
\item $\{$symmetric monoidal bicategories$\}\cong\{\mathsf{E}_{\infty}$-algebras in $\mathrm{BiCat}^{\times}\}$.
\end{enumerate}
These bijections are natural with respect to the obvious forgetful maps from bottom to top. The same applies to the corresponding 
notions of morphisms between them.

