 A similar calculation shows $\beta_3 = \beta_2$.
 The entries $D(\Sigma^{\csp})_i$ are computed using \eqref{eq:matrixD}:
 \begin{align*}
 D(\Sigma^{\csp})_2 &= -\zeta_3 \log(2\zeta_3 +23) - \zeta_3^{-1} \log(2\zeta_3^{-1} + 23),\\
